WEBVTT

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.310
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.700
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.670
My dad had a partner on his last hunt.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.250
The guy screwed up, got my dad killed.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.320
What does this have to do
-It was your father, Dean.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.970
Maybe that's what the demon's doing
-Pushing us, finding ways to break us.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:31.730
I'm Meg.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.040
She's possessed --A human
possessed by a demon.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.550
Key of Solomon --You get a demon
in one, theyre trapped, powerless.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.200
Before dad died, he told
something -Something about you.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.360
He said that I had to save you, and
if I couldnt, Id have to kill you.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.860
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.580
Am I supposed to go dark side?

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.440
I never said that.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.190
You're not careful; you will
have to waste me one day, Dean.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.880
Ellen, its me again.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.470
Any chance you've heard from him?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.090
I swear, its like looking
for my dad all over again.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.700
I'm losing my mind here.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.190
I've called him a thousand times.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.240
It's nothing but voice mail.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.990
I don't know where he went or why.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.640
Sam's just gone.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.780
Hang on.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.440
Sammy, where the hell are you?

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.380
Are you okay?

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.210
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:23.890
Calm down.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.610
Where are you?

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.210
Don't move.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.380
I'm on my way.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.930
Sam, its me.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.680
Sam!

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.030
Sam?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.560
Hey.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.030
Hey, Dean.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.530
Are you bleeding?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.670
I tried to wash it off.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:18.990
Oh, my god.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.270
I don't think its my blood.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:24.050
Whose is it?

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.100
I don't know.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.620
Sam, what the hell happened?

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:28.480
Dean...

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.350
I don't remember anything.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.610
What did you find out?

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.630
You checked in two days ago
under the name Richard sambora.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.320
I think the scariest part about this whole
thing is the fact that you're a bon jovi fan.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.220
Dean.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.550
Your room's been quiet.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.080
Nobody's noticed anything unusual.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.080
You mean no one saw me walking
around covered in blood?

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.100
Yeah, thats what I mean.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.830
Then how the hell did I get here?

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.600
What happened to me?

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.280
I don't know, but you're
okay, and that's what matters.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.050
Everything else, we can deal with.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:12.960
Oh, really?

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.440
'Cause what if I hurt someone or worse?

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.610
Sam.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.530
What if this is what
dad warned you about?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.490
Come on, man.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.500
Let's not jump the gun here.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.850
We don't know what happened.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.910
We got to treat this like any other job.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.400
What's the last thing you remember?

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.040
Me and you in that
motel room in west Texas.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.390
We went out to grab some burgers.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.700
West Texas -That was over a week ago.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.270
That's it.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.430
Next thing I knew, I was sitting here...

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.890
Bloody.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.340
I felt like I had been
asleep for a month.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.140
Okay, retrace your steps.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.110
Manager said you left yesterday
afternoon and never saw you come back.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.240
Hey.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.620
Recognize anything?

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.440
Not really.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.400
Wait.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:23.770
What?

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.960
I think I was here.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.070
You remember?

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.590
Not really. It just...

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.200
Feels familiar, you know?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.900
Try that one.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.760
Yeah.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.130
Okay.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.110
Wait.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.530
Please tell me you didn't steal this.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.610
More blood.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.370
Sam, backseat.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.700
You think I used this on someone?

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.590
I'm not thinking anything.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.500
Okay, now, this is disturbing.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.270
Come on, man.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.480
This couldn't have been you.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.360
It could have been someone else
-Somebody who, uh, smokes menthols.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.510
Hey, a gas receipts, a few towns over.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.100
All right, receipts for10
gallons at pump number 2.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.470
You getting any goose bumps yet?

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.790
"God, this looks familiar,"djavu vibes?

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.790
Maybe someone inside will remember you.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.670
Come on.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:31.210
You -Out of here.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:31.760
Now.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:32.740
I'm calling the cops.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.650
You talking to him?

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.900
Yeah, Im talking to him.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:39.240
Jerk comes in yesterday, stinking drunk,
grabs a 40 from the fridge, starts chugging it.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:39.930
This guy?

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.330
You're drinking malt liquor?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.080
Not after he whipped the
bottle at my friggin' head.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.240
This guy?

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.970
What, am I speaking Urdu?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:50.270
I'm really sorry if I did anything
tell your story walking, pal, okay?

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.260
Popo will be here in five.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:51.820
Wait.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.780
He's leaving.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.740
Put the phone down.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.090
Sam, go wait in the car.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.660
But, Dean  go wait in the car!

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.670
Okay, look, I just want to
talk to you that are it, okay?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.550
When he took off yesterday,
which way did he go?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.710
Why don't you ask him?

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.060
'Cause I'm asking you.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.660
Please, youd be doing
mea huge favor, okay?

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.310
Oh, do you a favor.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:19.310
Well, that is what I live for.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:24.690
You know, your buddy didn't pay for the booze
or the smokes, which he also illegally lit up.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:25.840
You saw him smoking?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.440
Yeah, guys a chimney.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.530
This, uh...

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:36.820
Ought to cover it.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.830
Hmm, its, uh, its
coming back to me now.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.780
He took two packs.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.750
Of course he did.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.790
Heent north on route
71, straight out of town.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.280
What's going on with you, sam, hmm?

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:12.460
The smoking, throwing bottles at people
-That sounds more like me than you.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:13.210
Dean, wait.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.360
Wait. Here.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:15.370
Turn down that road.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:15.850
What?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:16.450
I don't know how I know.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:17.390
I just do.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.000
Whoever lives here, Id say
they don't like surprises.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:01.890
Should we knock?

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.990
Yeah, I guess.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.440
Hey, Dean.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.430
I'm surprised the cops didnt show -Place
like this you'd think would have an alarm.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.050
Yeah, you would.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.170
Hit the lights.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.040
Dean, I did this.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:22.810
We don't know that.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:23.860
What else do you need?

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:26.820
How else do you explain the
car, the knife, the blood?

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:27.320
I don't know, man.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:28.540
Why don't you tell me?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:38.570
Even if you did do this, Im sure you had a reason -You
know, self-Defense, he was a bad son of a bitch --Something.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.260
He doesn't have any I.D.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.780
I need your lock pick.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:49.430
What?

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.680
I need your lock pick.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.000
Either this guys a
Unabomber -Or a hunter.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.370
Dean, I think I killed a hunter.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.790
Let's find out.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.810
Here we go.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.750
How do you erase this, huh?

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:20.920
Sam, come on.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.110
I need your help.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.590
I killed him, Dean.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.540
I just broke in and killed him.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:29.930
Listen to me.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.380
Whoever this guy is, hes a hunter, which means
other hunters are gonna look for his killer,

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.590
Which means we got to
cover our tracks, okay?

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.530
His name was Steve Wandell.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.930
This is a letter from his daughter.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.620
Wipe your prints. Then we go.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:23.190
All right, we get a couple hours' sleep, and
then we put this place in our rearview mirror.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.720
I know this is bad, okay?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.730
You got to snap out of it.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:32.590
Sam, say something.

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.570
Just get some sleep and
leave in the morning?

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.410
Murder, Dean
--That's what I did.

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.760
Maybe, okay?

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.470
Hey, we don't
--Shapeshifter.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:43.580
Oh, come on.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.240
You know it wasnt.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:44.930
You saw the tape.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.480
There was no eye flare, no distortion.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.560
But it wasn't you, all right?

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.240
Yeah, it might have been
you, but it wasn't you.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.090
Well, I think it was.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.300
I think maybe more than you know.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.890
What the hell does that mean?

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:06.090
For the last few weeks,
Ive been having...

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.450
I've been having these feelings.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:11.310
What feelings?

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.360
Rage...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:14.730
Hate.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.100
And I can't stop it.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:19.940
It just gets worse.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.650
Day by day, it gets worse.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:24.260
You never told me this.

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:27.650
I didn't want to scare you.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.330
Well, bang-Up job on that.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.610
Dean, the yellow-Eyed demon
-You know he has plans for me.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.620
And we both know that hes turned
other children into killers before, too.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.380
No one can control you but you.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.340
It sure doesn't seem like that, Dean.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:48.850
It feels like no matter what I do, slowly
but surely, Im just becoming --What?

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.730
Who I'm meant to be.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.020
You said it onceyourself, Dean.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.220
I got to face up to who I am.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:55.100
I didn't mean this!

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.450
But it's still true.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.670
You know that.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:58.730
Dad knew that, too.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.970
That's why he told you
if it ever came to this

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:01.920
Shut up, Sam.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.720
Dean, you promised him.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.690
You promised me.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:11.350
No.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:13.400
Listen to me.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:15.920
We're gonna figure this out, okay?

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.120
I mean, theres got to be a way, right?

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.530
Yeah, there is.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.050
I don't want to hurt anyone else.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:34.580
I don't want to hurt you.

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:38.230
You wont.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.570
Whatever this is, you can fight it.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.750
No, I cant...

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:46.710
Not forever.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:49.780
Here. You got to do it.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.380
You know, Ive tried so
hard to keep you safe.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:09.940
I know.

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:20.710
I cant.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.260
I'd rather die.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:30.940
No.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.330
You'll live.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:50.090
You'll live to regret this.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:19.960
It's past your checkout.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:32.220
What?

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:35.320
It's past checkout, and I have a
couple here that need your room.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.940
Yeah, Ill bet they do.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:41.430
What time is it?

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:42.600
12:30.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.340
The guy that was with
me --Have you seen him?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:52.030
Yeah, he left before dawn in your car, and you should have
gone with him because now I'm gonna have to charge you extra.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.270
Oh, son of a bitch.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.660
It's just policy, sir.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.280
I need to use your computer.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.960
Why would I let you use my computer?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.160
Hi.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:09.570
Uh, so sorry to bother you, but, uh, my
son snuck out of the house last night and,

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:12.080
Uh, went to a Justin Timberlake concert.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.030
What?

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:15.770
Yeah.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.810
Justin is quite the triple threat.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.790
Uh, anyway, hes not back
yet, and I'm starting to worry.

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:25.520
Right, yeah, boys will be boys.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.790
But, see, Sammy is a...

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:32.100
Diabetic, and if he doesn't get his
insulin, then I just --I have to find him.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.270
Please, Im begging you.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.390
No, no, no, Im on
the website right now.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:40.620
I just need to activate
the GPS on his cellphone.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.120
Yeah, right there.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.680
Duluth, Minnesota.

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.800
Yeah, that is a long
way to go for a concert.

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:49.900
I appreciate your help.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:57.870
Night.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:58.940
Thank you.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.160
Sorry, were closing up.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.450
How about just one for the road?

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.220
Well, youre about the last
person I'd expect to see.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:15.760
Well...

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.990
I guess I'm full of surprises.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:22.950
So, can I get a beer?

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:24.930
Sure.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.630
One beer.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.330
So, howd you find me?

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.750
Well, uh, its kind of
what we do, you know?

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.620
Speaking of "we,?Wheres Dean?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:49.910
Couldn't make it.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:53.980
So, what are you doing here, Sam?

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.050
We didn't exactly part
on the best of terms.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:19:59.620
Right.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.690
Thats why I'm here.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:07.560
I kind of wanted to see if we
could square things, you know?

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:09.680
That looks like it hurts.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:12.540
No.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:13.940
No, just...

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.580
Had a run-In with a hot stove.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.650
So, you were saying something
about squaring things?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.670
Yeah.

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:30.010
Look, I know how you feel about my
dad, and I can't say I blame you.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:37.840
He was obsessed, consumed with hunting, and
he didn't care who got caught in the crossfire.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.040
And I guess that included your dad.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:44.440
But that was my father.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:45.720
That's not me.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:48.990
What about Dean?

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:53.950
Well, Deans more like my
father than I am, but he...

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:01.360
Boy...

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.670
Youre really carrying a
torch for him, arent you?

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:08.820
I'll take that as a yes.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.140
It's too bad.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.170
'Cause, see, Dean, he
likes you, sure, but...

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:18.650
Not in the way you'd want.

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:26.640
I mean, maybe as kind of a little sister,
but romance -That's just out of the question.

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.800
He Kind of thinks youre
a schoolgirl, you know?

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:35.940
I'm not trying to hurt you, Jo.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.600
I -I'm telling you cause I care.

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:41.290
That's real kind of you, Sam.

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:43.370
I mean it.

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:49.830
I care about you a lot.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.100
Sam, whats going on?

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:57.190
I can be more to you, Jo.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:58.940
Maybe you should leave.

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:03.550
Okay.

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:14.980
Sam, get off me!

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:16.740
Sam, get off me!

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:17.800
Let go.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.750
Jo, Jo, Jo.

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:32.940
Sam, no, pleases!

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:33.760
Please.

00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:49.340
It didn't have to be this way.

00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:53.450
Maybe it did.

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:09.890
What the hell's going on?

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:11.940
What are you doing?

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:17.260
So, what exactly did your mom
tell you about how your dad died?

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:19.080
You're not Sam.

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:20.390
Don't be so sure about that.

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:21.420
Answer the question....

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:28.860
Come on.

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:32.400
It's me.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:33.940
You can tell me anything.

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:35.060
You know that.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:38.450
Answer the question.

00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:41.240
Fine.

00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:42.370
Fine.

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:47.740
Our dads were in California
-Devil's gate reservoir.

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:50.140
They were setting a trap
for some kind of hell spawn.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:54.630
John was hiding, waiting,
and my dad was bait.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.950
That's just like john.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:01.270
Oh, I bet he dangled
bill like meat on a hook.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:02.060
Then what?

00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:06.050
The thing showed up.

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:10.880
John got too eager, jumped out too soon,
and got my dad exposed out in the open.

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:14.110
The thing turned around...

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:16.310
And killed him.

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:21.690
Not quite.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:25.600
What?

00:24:26.120 --> 00:24:26.610
What?

00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:28.820
See, it hurt him.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:31.250
It didn't kill him.

00:24:33.990 --> 00:24:35.690
You really don't know the truth, do you?

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:39.120
I bet your momdoesn't, either.

00:24:39.590 --> 00:24:40.350
Know what?

00:24:40.640 --> 00:24:41.700
You see, bill...

00:24:43.360 --> 00:24:44.480
Was all clawed up.

00:24:46.160 --> 00:24:47.950
He was holding his insides in his hands.

00:24:49.360 --> 00:24:50.530
He was gargling and...

00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:54.030
Praying to see you and
Ellen one more time.

00:24:55.700 --> 00:24:56.890
So my dad...

00:24:59.330 --> 00:25:00.510
Killed him.

00:25:02.340 --> 00:25:04.730
He put him out of his
misery like a sick dog.

00:25:04.790 --> 00:25:05.330
You're lying.

00:25:05.330 --> 00:25:05.770
I'm not.

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:06.760
It's true.

00:25:07.210 --> 00:25:10.570
My daddy shot your daddy in the head

00:25:10.570 --> 00:25:11.900
How could you know that?

00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:12.870
I hear things.

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:16.480
Why are you doing this to me?

00:25:16.480 --> 00:25:17.710
Like daddy, like daughter.

00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:18.450
You're bait.

00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:19.280
Open up.

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:21.970
That's a girl.

00:25:23.290 --> 00:25:24.070
Sam!

00:25:25.830 --> 00:25:27.400
I begged you to stop me, Dean!

00:25:27.630 --> 00:25:28.510
Put the knife down, damn it.

00:25:28.510 --> 00:25:30.190
I told you I can't fight it!

00:25:30.630 --> 00:25:32.960
My head feels like
its on fire, all right?

00:25:34.030 --> 00:25:37.200
Dean, kill me, or I'm gonna kill her.

00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:39.020
Please.

00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:40.200
You'd be doing me a favor.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:42.720
Shoot me.

00:25:46.130 --> 00:25:47.160
Shoot me!

00:25:56.460 --> 00:25:57.780
No, sammy.Come on.

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:03.190
What the hells wrong with you, Dean?

00:26:04.550 --> 00:26:07.710
Are you that scared of being
alone that you'd rather let Jo die?

00:26:11.070 --> 00:26:13.130
That's holy water, you
demonic son of a bitch!

00:26:26.500 --> 00:26:28.800
He was possessed?

00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:33.200
Dean!

00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:55.200
So, who are you? I got lots of names.

00:27:02.600 --> 00:27:04.800
You've been in Sam since
he Disappeared, havent you?

00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:10.600
Should have seen your face when you
thought He murdered that guy. Pathetic.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:19.900
Why didn't you kill me?
You had a dozen chances.

00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:28.100
No, that would have been too
easy. Where's the fun in that?

00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:34.000
See, this was a test. I wanted to see If
I could push you far enough to waste Sam.

00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:38.200
I should have known you
wouldn't have the sack.

00:27:38.300 --> 00:27:40.700
Anyway, funs over now.

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:45.000
Well, I hope you got your kicks
'cause you're gonna pay hell for this.

00:27:45.100 --> 00:27:49.900
How? You can't hurt me
- Not without hurting your little brother.

00:27:51.100 --> 00:27:59.500
See, I think you're gonna die, Dean
- You and every other hunter I can find.

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:07.100
One look at Sams dewy, sensitive eyes,
And they'll let me right in that door.

00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:20.600
This is Dean. Leave a message.

00:29:49.200 --> 00:29:49.900
Dean!

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:51.900
Dean!

00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:57.500
Take it easy.

00:29:58.400 --> 00:30:01.100
Where's Sam? I don't know.
Ive been looking for you.

00:30:01.200 --> 00:30:03.800
Come on. Get up.

00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:14.100
Okay. Dont be a baby!

00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:15.200
God.

00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:20.200
All right, almost. All
right, got it. Got it.

00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:30.200
God, youre a butcher. You're welcome.

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.900
All right, are we done? Would you
give me two minutes to patch you up?

00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:36.800
You can't help Sam if
you're bleeding to death.

00:30:38.800 --> 00:30:41.700
So, how did you know
that he was possessed?

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:47.400
I didnt. I just knew that
It couldn't have been him.

00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:50.700
Hey, Dean. Yeah.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:56.100
I know demons lie, But do
they ever tell the truth, too?

00:30:58.500 --> 00:31:03.700
Yeah, sometimes, I guess, especially
If they know it'll mess with your head.

00:31:06.700 --> 00:31:08.300
Why do you ask?

00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:12.700
Nothing. It doesn't matter.

00:31:12.800 --> 00:31:14.900
So, do you have any idea?
Where he's headed to next?

00:31:15.100 --> 00:31:20.300
So far, hes been going after the nearest hunter,
So, the closest one I know is in South Dakota.

00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:22.600
Okay, good. Im done. Lets go.

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:28.600
You're not coming. The hell
I'm not. Im a part of this now.

00:31:28.800 --> 00:31:34.000
I can't say it more plain than this you try and
follow me, And I'll tie you right back to that post.

00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:37.200
This is my fight. Im not
getting Your blood on my hands.

00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:39.000
That's just how it's gonna be.

00:31:42.900 --> 00:31:46.600
Wait. Here.

00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:51.300
Take these. Theyll help with the pain.

00:31:54.500 --> 00:31:55.400
Thanks.

00:31:58.800 --> 00:32:00.800
I'll call you later, okay?

00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:08.400
No, you wont.

00:32:29.600 --> 00:32:31.200
Damn it.

00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:46.000
Sam. Hey, bobby.

00:32:46.200 --> 00:32:49.600
It's been a while. Come on in.

00:32:57.400 --> 00:33:02.100
So, what brings you? Working a job nearby,
and I thought I'd stop in and say hey.

00:33:02.300 --> 00:33:05.300
Where's Dean?

00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:08.200
Holed up somewhere with
a girl and a 12-Pack.

00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:14.500
Oh, yeah? Is she pretty? You ask
me, hes in way over his head.

00:33:17.100 --> 00:33:18.600
Well, its good to see you.

00:33:20.800 --> 00:33:21.600
To john.

00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:25.600
To dad.

00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:42.600
What'd you do? Little
holy water in the beer.

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:48.100
Sam never would have noticed,
But, then, youre not Sam, are you?

00:33:48.300 --> 00:33:51.300
Don't try to con a con man.

00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:02.100
Ugh!

00:34:20.800 --> 00:34:24.500
Dean. Back from the dead.

00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:27.300
Getting to be a regular
thing for you, isnt it?

00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:29.200
Like a cockroach.

00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:31.900
How about I smack that smart-Ass
Right out of your mouth?

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:33.000
Careful now.

00:34:33.100 --> 00:34:38.200
Wouldn't want to bruise this fine packaging
Oh, dont worry. This isn't gonna hurt Sam much.

00:34:39.100 --> 00:34:40.800
You, on the other hand...

00:34:44.700 --> 00:34:47.300
Feel like talking now?

00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:50.000
Sam's still my meat puppet.

00:34:50.800 --> 00:34:54.700
I'll make him bite off his tongue.
No, you won't be in him long enough.

00:34:55.300 --> 00:34:56.300
Bobby.

00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:11.500
Ee, whatever bitch-Boy master plan you demons Are
cooking up, youre not getting Sam, you understand me?

00:35:11.700 --> 00:35:14.700
'Cause I'm gonna kill
every one of you first.

00:35:26.500 --> 00:35:31.300
You really think that's what this is about
- The master plan?

00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:36.100
I don't give a rat's ass
about the master plan.

00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:43.900
Oops.Doesn't seem to be working.

00:35:44.400 --> 00:35:46.600
See, I learned a few new tricks.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:06.200
This isn't going like I
pictured. What's going on, bobby?

00:36:09.400 --> 00:36:11.500
It's a binding link!

00:36:11.800 --> 00:36:15.500
It's like a lock. Its locked
Itself inside Sams body.

00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:18.100
What the hell do we do? I don't know!

00:36:27.700 --> 00:36:30.800
There. Thats better.

00:36:39.700 --> 00:36:43.400
You know when people want to
describe The worst possible thing...

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:45.800
They say it's like hell?

00:36:46.700 --> 00:36:51.000
Well, theres a reason for
that. Hell is like, uh...

00:36:53.800 --> 00:36:57.800
Well, its like hell, even for demons.

00:36:58.900 --> 00:37:04.600
It's a prison made of bone
and Flesh and blood and fear.

00:37:08.100 --> 00:37:10.800
And you sent me back there.

00:37:11.900 --> 00:37:16.000
Meg. No...Not anymore.

00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:17.900
Now I'm Sam.

00:37:20.300 --> 00:37:21.700
By the way...

00:37:23.100 --> 00:37:26.500
I saw your dad there. He says "howdy."

00:37:27.100 --> 00:37:33.200
All that I had to hold on to was that I would
Climb out one day and that I was gonna torture you,

00:37:33.500 --> 00:37:37.500
Nice and slow, like pulling
the wings off an insect.

00:37:38.100 --> 00:37:42.900
But whatever I do to you, its nothing
compared To what you do to yourself, is it?

00:37:43.400 --> 00:37:45.500
I can see it in your eyes, Dean.

00:37:45.800 --> 00:37:49.300
You're worthless. You
couldn't save your dad

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:54.800
And deep down, you know that
You can't save your brother.

00:37:55.700 --> 00:37:57.900
They'd have been better off without you.

00:38:27.100 --> 00:38:28.600
Sammy?

00:38:32.600 --> 00:38:34.800
Did I miss anything?

00:38:48.100 --> 00:38:51.500
By the way, you really
look like crap, Dean.

00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:54.200
Yeah, right back at you.

00:39:00.100 --> 00:39:01.500
What is it, bobby?

00:39:02.400 --> 00:39:05.600
You boys ever hear of a
hunter Named Steve Wandell?

00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:08.800
Why do you ask?

00:39:09.500 --> 00:39:15.500
Just heard from a friend, wandells dead
- Murdered in his own house.

00:39:17.100 --> 00:39:19.500
You wouldn't know anything about that.

00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:22.300
No, sir.Never heard of the guy. Dean.

00:39:22.400 --> 00:39:24.900
Good. Keep it that way.

00:39:25.100 --> 00:39:28.800
Wandell's buddies are looking for
Someone or something to string up.

00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:31.700
They're not gonna slow
down to listen to reason.

00:39:32.100 --> 00:39:34.100
You understand what I'm saying?

00:39:35.600 --> 00:39:37.500
We better hit the road...

00:39:37.800 --> 00:39:40.700
If, uh, you can remember
where we parked the car.

00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:42.800
Here. Take these.

00:39:45.500 --> 00:39:50.400
What are they? Charms.
Theyll fend off possession.

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:54.700
That demon's still out there. This will
Stop it from getting back up in you.

00:39:54.900 --> 00:39:58.700
That sounds vaguely dirty,
but, uh, thanks. You're welcome.

00:39:59.200 --> 00:40:03.000
You boys be careful, now. You too.

00:40:28.300 --> 00:40:30.400
You okay?

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:33.700
Sam?

00:40:35.500 --> 00:40:36.800
Is that you in there?

00:40:41.300 --> 00:40:43.600
I was awake for some of it, Dean.

00:40:45.800 --> 00:40:53.300
I watched myself kill Wandell with my own
two hands. I saw the light go out in his eyes.

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:57.200
It must have been awful.

00:40:59.600 --> 00:41:01.600
That's not my point.

00:41:03.300 --> 00:41:05.700
I almost carved up jota.

00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:08.500
But no matter what I
did, you wouldn't shoot.

00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:11.600
It was the right move,
sam.It wasn't you.

00:41:11.700 --> 00:41:15.600
Yeah, this time. What about next time?

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:27.000
Sam, when dad told me that I might have to
kill you, It was only if I couldn't save you.

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:30.500
Now, if it's the last thing
I do, I'm gonna save you.

00:41:39.000 --> 00:41:39.400
What?

00:41:40.400 --> 00:41:41.500
Nothing.

00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:44.500
Dean, what?

00:41:44.600 --> 00:41:50.300
Dude, you, like, full-On had a girl
inside you for, Like, a whole week.

00:41:53.300 --> 00:41:54.700
That's pretty naughty.



